				<!-- Home widget row size, was hardcoded at 15 in nine places. It is a
				     stepper on a plain button, with no dialog anywhere: LEFT steps
				     down and stops at 5, RIGHT steps up and stops at 25, and OK
				     cycles forward and wraps 25 back to 5. Left and right are
				     directional, so a wrap on them would swing the whole range on one
				     press with no cue; OK is not directional and there is only one of
				     it, so it has to wrap or the row goes dead at 25.
				     Every other route Kodi offers is closed, all measured against the
				     Kodi 22 source, so do not "improve" this back into one of them:
				       - Addon.OpenSettings on a skin is refused. CSkinInfo::HasSettings
				         and HasUserSettings return false unconditionally (Skin.h:216-217,
				         "Don't handle skin settings like normal addon settings"), which
				         is why Kodi answers "This add-on can't be configured".
				       - There is no slider or spinner builtin. SkinBuiltins.cpp:725-746
				         is the complete list, and Skin.SetNumeric always opens a keypad
				         and never clamps.
				       - spincontrolex in a skin's own window is a costume.
				         GUIControlFactory.cpp:1693-1706 builds it with no items and
				         parses no tag that would add any, and SetClickActions is not
				         called for it, so its <onclick> is discarded in silence.
				       - Sliders bind to a hardcoded whitelist of seek, pvr.seek and
				         volume (GUISliderControl.cpp:26-29).
				     Builtins in a navigation slot are legitimate and already shipped in
				     this skin at MusicOSD.xml:281-282. CGUIWindow::OnMove runs
				     ExecuteActions before GetNavigation (GUIWindow.cpp:970-971), and
				     ExecuteActions skips integers while GetNavigation skips
				     non-integers (GUIAction.cpp:66-67, 90), so the two never collide.
				     ExecuteActions is also two pass, snapshotting every condition
				     before running any of them (GUIAction.cpp:60-69), which is what
				     makes the OK wrap safe: no step can cascade into the next.
				     THE ONE COST: this control defines its own left and right, and a
				     vertical grouplist only applies its own left and right to a child
				     with replace=false (GUIControlGroupList.cpp:351-352, and
				     GUIControl.cpp:528-533 where replace=false means "only if unset"),
				     so left no longer walks back to the category list 9000 from THIS
				     row. Up and down still move normally, and both neighbours keep
				     left, so the row is escapable. -->
				<control type="button" id="709">
					<label>$LOCALIZE[31616]</label>
					<include>DefaultSettingButton</include>
					<label2>$VAR[HomeItemLimitVar]</label2>
					<onclick condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),25)">Skin.SetString(home_items,5)</onclick>
					<onclick condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),20)">Skin.SetString(home_items,25)</onclick>
					<onclick condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),15)">Skin.SetString(home_items,20)</onclick>
					<onclick condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),10)">Skin.SetString(home_items,15)</onclick>
					<onclick condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),5)">Skin.SetString(home_items,10)</onclick>
					<onright condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),20)">Skin.SetString(home_items,25)</onright>
					<onright condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),15)">Skin.SetString(home_items,20)</onright>
					<onright condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),10)">Skin.SetString(home_items,15)</onright>
					<onright condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),5)">Skin.SetString(home_items,10)</onright>
					<onleft condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),25)">Skin.SetString(home_items,20)</onleft>
					<onleft condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),20)">Skin.SetString(home_items,15)</onleft>
					<onleft condition="String.IsEqual(Skin.String(home_items),15)">Skin.SetString(home_items,10)</onleft>
